      ],
      "source": "https://www.worldatlas.com/cities/this-maine-town-is-older-than-the-state-itself.html",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Pepperrell Cove, a walkable historic district, hosts the Lady Pepperrell House and William Pepperrell House, landmarks of Georgian architecture.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1,
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.worldatlas.com/cities/this-maine-town-is-older-than-the-state-itself.html",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Kittery sits at Maine’s southern tip along the Piscataqua River and is known as the “Gateway to Maine.”.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
